2026-11-02  Bryant Frankford  <nathanielfrankford@gmail.com>

	topology paint: a drawing and painting program built into topology,
	in C, for Windows, Linux and macOS, with pen pressure, brushes,
	layers, the usual file formats and mods (Bryant's request, 2026-11-02).
	* paint/: the program (src/core without SDL, src/app with SDL3),
	the mod API (include/tpaint_mod.h) and three example mods, brushes,
	palettes, build.bat and build.sh, CMakeLists.txt, tests, README.md
	with screenshots, docs/MODDING.md, docs/LESSONS-LEARNED.md.
	* RECIPE.org: what goes in (SDL 3.2.26 by sha256, stb); test.sh
	runs paint/tests/run.sh and its --prove-red.
	* bin/test.sh: tangled again.
	* examples/inputloop/: topology-paint, in topology and by bryant.
	* spec/fixtures/examples.json: made again.
	* README.org, NEWS, AUTHORS, REUSE.toml, LICENSES/: the new part
	and its licences (MIT OR Unlicense for stb, Bitstream-Vera for the
	baked DejaVu glyphs).
	* .github/workflows/paint.yml: build and test paint on Windows
	(MSVC), macOS and Linux.

